# Forcefield, activated for exactly {1} as the attackers are declared, has no unblocked creature to choose - before blockers
# are declared an attacking creature is neither blocked nor unblocked (CR 509.1h) - so it asks nothing and does nothing.
# Activated again once blockers are declared, it offers only the unblocked creatures (not the blocked trampler: the ruling),
# and leaves 1 of the chosen Elite Vanguard's 2 combat damage, while Garruk's Companion's 3 is dealt in full (CR 609.7a,
# 615.8, 615.1). The two attackers' powers differ, so a shield on the wrong one, or on both, or leaving another amount, shows.
[Bot1 Deck]
Forcefield
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Island
Phyrexian Walker
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Garruk's Companion
Elite Vanguard
Charging Badger
Island x20

